  "checklist": [
    "Each row shows its officer's portrait, his rank and status under the name, and his traits as the game's icons (compare three officers with the game's own general window)",
    "The column heads show the game's attack, defence, planning and logistics icons; a click on each sorts, a second click turns the order",
    "A click anywhere on an officer's portrait or name opens his file and marks his row, the name in yellow",
    "The file: portrait, rank and status, the five level plates with their icons, Divisions/Battalions/Fighting/Armoured/Planning against the game's army view",
    "Traits: icon and name of each, and \"N of M he can take\"; note what num_max_traits gives",
    "Planning: is it shown as a percentage (0 to 100%)?",
    "Award... shows the country's medals over the decorations and diary cards; Award one; the plate says awarded with the date; Back to his file shows the medal on the rack at full size and in his row at half size",
    "Take back last; choosing another officer ends the Award mode",
    "An admiral (Raeder): manoeuvring and coordination icons, Ships and the four ship kinds",
    "error.log: no line about has_trait, a sprite GFX_trait_ or GFX_1440p_medal_, or an array index",
    "E7 with Road to 56: every row's face is the officer's own, as the game's Officer Corps lists and commander picker show him: Wilhelm Keitel and Franz Halder (texture files of Road to 56, the unknown leader before E7), Rundstedt, Manstein; the admirals Raeder, Doenitz and Otto Ciliax (texture file) as in the Officer Corps' Admirals list",
    "E7: after mod1440_chk_e7_generals (one day, or a click on All): Heinrich Himmler (texture file), Martin Bormann and Wilhelm Canaris (his civilian portrait, as the commander picker) as rows with their own faces",
    "E7: click Keitel: his file shows his own face at full size (156x210); click Himmler: the same in his file",
    "E7: choose an officer, effect mod1440_chk_e7_retire, one day, filter Former: his row and his file show the table's portrait (or the unknown leader for one the table lacks), not the game's unknown man; mod1440_chk_e7_log: 'file 0'. game.log at the effect: 'MOD1440 e7 retired <name>: is_unit_leader no' (not known before; 'yes' is a finding: the pages would draw him as the unknown man)",
    "E7 gate B: the faces hold on a day after the start without opening the Officers page first: close the Records on the War Diary tab on day 1 (they reopen on the page they were closed on), run one day, open them, then select Poznan on the map: the officers' faces in the diary and on Poznan's state card are the game's (decided by is_unit_leader, not by the day last seen)",
    "E7: the faces scale as before (34x46 in the rows) and stay on their rows while the list scrolls; error.log: no line naming 'portrait', mod1440_of_c_ul or is_unit_leader"
  ],
